(CLI-01: Basic Usage - `vox <source.vox> [options]` - the compiler takes
 exactly one source file and zero or more options. This is the minimal
 case: no options at all, output defaults to the source stem with no
 extension (`hello.vox` -> `hello`). check-probes.sh's own harness (`vox
 probe.vox -o work/name`) exercises this same basic form on every probe
 in every ledger; this file is the CLI-specific record of the no-options
 default-name case, hand-run separately since check-probes.sh always
 supplies its own -o.
 Hand-run separately:
   $ vox hello.vox
   $ ls hello
   -rwxr-xr-x ... hello
   $ ./hello
   Hello, World!
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox CLI-01.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   Hello, World!
)
Print "Hello, World!".
